  "id": "Compound::DB00898 - Gene::125",
  "verbalization": "Ethanol and Adh1b are linked through a series of molecular interactions that involve the enzyme Adh1a. Ethanol binds to Adh1a, which then participates in multiple metabolic processes, including alcohol dehydrogenation and ethanol oxidation. These activities are ultimately participated by Adh1b, suggesting a functional relationship between Adh1a and Adh1b in the context of ethanol metabolism. The evidence from the three paths indicates that Adh1b is a downstream participant in the metabolic pathways initiated by ethanol binding to Adh1a, highlighting a potential role in the enzymatic conversion of ethanol to acetaldehyde. The integration of these pathways underscores the importance of Adh1a as a central mediator in the interaction between ethanol and Adh1b, emphasizing a mechanistic link that is consistent across different metabolic contexts.",
